			"Message": "style(Grove): Reformat Transport method chains for readability\n\nApply multi-line formatting to the `connect`, `send`, and `close` method implementations within `Source/Transport/Strategy.rs`. This restructures the `.await` and `.map_err` call chains across all `Transport` variants—including `gRPC`, `IPC`, `WASM`, and `WebSocket`—to align with the organization's formatting standards for asynchronous code.\n\nThis ensures consistent styling across the transport layer and improves the clarity of error handling logic by distinctively separating the method invocations from their respective error mapping blocks.",
			"SHA": "ce5b687b0f49da89b05e72ce27c330fb13b331dd"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-28T13:22:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				78,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Grove): Implement WebSocket transport via Mist protocol\n\nIntroduce a new high-frequency transport layer for Grove that leverages the Mist JSON-RPC-over-WS protocol. This enables extension host components to communicate with the Mountain backend over local WebSockets, providing a low-latency alternative to the existing gRPC and IPC transports.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Add the `Mist` workspace dependency and a `websocket` feature gate to `Cargo.toml`.\n- Implement `MistTransport` in `Source/Transport/MistTransport.rs`, wrapping the `Mist::WebSocket::Client` and fulfilling the `TransportStrategy` contract for `invoke` and `notify` patterns.\n- Extend the `TransportType` and `Transport` enums in `Source/Transport/Strategy.rs` to support the `WebSocket` variant, including updated `Display` and `FromStr` logic.\n- Add the `CreateWebSocketTransport` factory function to `Source/Transport/mod.rs` to facilitate unified transport instantiation.\n\nThis ensures Grove can participate in high-frequency Sky ↔ Mountain communication streams while maintaining strict alignment with the project's PascalCase naming conventions and effect-based transport architecture.",
			"SHA": "44b37d0f746bccf9af896b5721c8eb261f17f341"
		},
